    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Subsection 4AA(1A)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015#sch-1-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1A) If the amount of a penalty unit is indexed under subsection (3), the\nMinister must, by notifiable instrument, publish the amount of a\npenalty unit. However, a failure by the Minister to do so does not\ninvalidate the indexation.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1A) If the amount of a penalty unit is indexed under subsection (3), the\nMinister must, by notifiable instrument, publish the amount of a\npenalty unit. However, a failure by the Minister to do so does not\ninvalidate the indexation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d0428f2151c58f5886bf8769d8b23aeb85429b4544d6c6e4bd17dd56c872762a",
      "skos:note": "Publish penalty unit amount by notifiable instrument.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015#sch-1-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Subsection 4AA(1A)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1A) If the amount of a penalty unit is indexed under subsection (3), the\nMinister must, by notifiable instrument, publish the amount of a\npenalty unit. However, a failure by the Minister to do so does not\ninvalidate the indexation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must publish penalty unit amount.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 At the end of section 4AA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015#sch-1-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nIndexation of penalty unit\n\n(3) On 1 July 2018 and each third 1 July following that day (an\nindexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is\nreplaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:\nIndexation factor\nDollar amount\nfor the indexation day\nimmediately before the indexation day\n\n\n(4) The indexation factor for an indexation day is the number worked\nout using the following formula:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00088\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Penalty Unit) Act 2015\nNo. 88, 2015\n\nIndex number for the reference quarter\nIndex number for the base quarter\n\nwhere:\nbase quarter means the March quarter 3 years before the reference\nquarter.\nindex number, for a quarter, means the All Groups Consumer\nPrice Index number (being the weighted average of the 8 capital\ncities) published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter.\nMarch quarter means a quarter ending on 31 March.\nreference quarter means the March quarter immediately before the\nindexation day.\n\n(5) An indexation factor is to be calculated to 3 decimal places\n(rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more).\n\n(6) Amounts worked out under subsection (3) are to be rounded to the\nnearest whole dollar (rounding 50 cents upwards).\n\n(7) Calculations under subsection (4):\n\n(a) are to be made using only the index numbers published in\nterms of the most recently published index reference period;\nand\n\n(b) are to be made disregarding index numbers that are published\nin substitution for previously published index numbers\n(except where the substituted numbers are published to take\naccount of changes in the index reference period).\nApplication of indexed penalty unit\n\n(8) If the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is increased in\naccordance with subsection (3), the increased amount only applies\nto offences committed on or after the indexation day.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nIndexation of penalty unit\n\n(3) On 1 July 2018 and each third 1 July following that day (an\nindexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is\nreplaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:\nIndexation factor\nDollar amount\nfor the indexation day\nimmediately before the indexation day\n\n\n(4) The indexation factor for an indexation day is the number worked\nout using the following formula:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00088\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Penalty Unit) Act 2015\nNo. 88, 2015\n\nIndex number for the reference quarter\nIndex number for the base quarter\n\nwhere:\nbase quarter means the March quarter 3 years before the reference\nquarter.\nindex number, for a quarter, means the All Groups Consumer\nPrice Index number (being the weighted average of the 8 capital\ncities) published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter.\nMarch quarter means a quarter ending on 31 March.\nreference quarter means the March quarter immediately before the\nindexation day.\n\n(5) An indexation factor is to be calculated to 3 decimal places\n(rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more).\n\n(6) Amounts worked out under subsection (3) are to be rounded to the\nnearest whole dollar (rounding 50 cents upwards).\n\n(7) Calculations under subsection (4):\n\n(a) are to be made using only the index numbers published in\nterms of the most recently published index reference period;\nand\n\n(b) are to be made disregarding index numbers that are published\nin substitution for previously published index numbers\n(except where the substituted numbers are published to take\naccount of changes in the index reference period).\nApplication of indexed penalty unit\n\n(8) If the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is increased in\naccordance with subsection (3), the increased amount only applies\nto offences committed on or after the indexation day.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "87b239da8ebb8d1dcab1bf58f738a0dbb3551cb86639300fcc22e1b3bc1d6ff8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015#sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 At the end of section 4AA",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nIndexation of penalty unit\n\n(3) On 1 July 2018 and each third 1 July following that day (an\nindexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is\nreplaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:\nIndexation factor\nDollar amount\nfor the indexation day\nimmediately before the indexation day\n\n\n(4) The indexation factor for an indexation day is the number worked\nout using the following formula:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00088\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Penalty Unit) Act 2015\nNo. 88, 2015\n\nIndex number for the reference quarter\nIndex number for the base quarter\n\nwhere:\nbase quarter means the March quarter 3 years before the reference\nquarter.\nindex number, for a quarter, means the All Groups Consumer\nPrice Index number (being the weighted average of the 8 capital\ncities) published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter.\nMarch quarter means a quarter ending on 31 March.\nreference quarter means the March quarter immediately before the\nindexation day.\n\n(5) An indexation factor is to be calculated to 3 decimal places\n(rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more).\n\n(6) Amounts worked out under subsection (3) are to be rounded to the\nnearest whole dollar (rounding 50 cents upwards).\n\n(7) Calculations under subsection (4):\n\n(a) are to be made using only the index numbers published in\nterms of the most recently published index reference period;\nand\n\n(b) are to be made disregarding index numbers that are published\nin substitution for previously published index numbers\n(except where the substituted numbers are published to take\naccount of changes in the index reference period).\nApplication of indexed penalty unit\n\n(8) If the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is increased in\naccordance with subsection (3), the increased amount only applies\nto offences committed on or after the indexation day."
    },
