      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The indexation factor for an indexation day is the number worked\nout using the following formula:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00088\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Penalty Unit) Act 2015\nNo. 88, 2015\n\nIndex number for the reference quarter\nIndex number for the base quarter\n\nwhere:\nbase quarter means the March quarter 3 years before the reference\nquarter.\nindex number, for a quarter, means the All Groups Consumer\nPrice Index number (being the weighted average of the 8 capital\ncities) published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter.\nMarch quarter means a quarter ending on 31 March.\nreference quarter means the March quarter immediately before the\nindexation day.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The indexation factor for an indexation day is the number worked\nout using the following formula:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00088\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Penalty Unit) Act 2015\nNo. 88, 2015\n\nIndex number for the reference quarter\nIndex number for the base quarter\n\nwhere:\nbase quarter means the March quarter 3 years before the reference\nquarter.\nindex number, for a quarter, means the All Groups Consumer\nPrice Index number (being the weighted average of the 8 capital\ncities) published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter.\nMarch quarter means a quarter ending on 31 March.\nreference quarter means the March quarter immediately before the\nindexation day.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "248235e171f5889c7ef83cd1de111a36aaec7b77b096c388443a92332dd6a76f",
      "skos:note": "Defines indexation factor formula for an indexation day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-penalty-unit-act-2015#sch-1-sec-4-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(4) At the end of section 4AA",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The indexation factor for an indexation day is the number worked\nout using the following formula:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00088\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Penalty Unit) Act 2015\nNo. 88, 2015\n\nIndex number for the reference quarter\nIndex number for the base quarter\n\nwhere:\nbase quarter means the March quarter 3 years before the reference\nquarter.\nindex number, for a quarter, means the All Groups Consumer\nPrice Index number (being the weighted average of the 8 capital\ncities) published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter.\nMarch quarter means a quarter ending on 31 March.\nreference quarter means the March quarter immediately before the\nindexation day."
    },
